id: pm-rnpmtp
title: Renew pinned pnpm Windows shell-launcher compatibility after dependency cooldown
description: "PR 1375 review identifies the locked pnpm 11.10.0 shell launcher using POSIX NODE_PATH when selecting Windows node.exe. The repository .txt templates only compare actual installed output and do not generate launchers. Upstream pnpm 11.28.1 also fixes Windows CMD percent-path handling and Cygwin target paths: https://github.com/pnpm/pnpm/releases/tag/v11.28.1. npm reports publication 2026-09-28T07:33:45.016Z, so that version first satisfies the unchanged seven-day cooldown on 2026-10-05T07:33:45.016Z; 11.28.2 is published later the same day. Evaluate a then-eligible supported version with real mixed-runtime fixtures instead of changing comparison templates independently of the installed generator. The verification edge to pm-q1ke preserves the completed pinned-installer bootstrap invariants when this future renewal is undertaken."
type: Chore
status: closed
priority: 2
tags[4]: compatibility,pnpm,tooling,windows
created_at: "2026-10-03T03:44:58.496Z"
updated_at: "2026-10-18T04:38:50.014Z"
closed_at: "2026-10-18T04:35:38.649Z"
completed_at: "2026-10-18T04:35:38.649Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 180
acceptance_criteria: "Retain the seven-day dependency cooldown; align packageManager and every CI/release/example pnpm pin; inspect actual published generator types/source and renew complete templates from real installation; run Windows Git Bash/Cygwin node.exe and POSIX Node dependency-resolution controls; verify quoted/percent paths, exact inventory, complete source coverage and all existing mandatory gates"
goal: Portable audited development tooling
objective: Renew pinned generator output and prove Windows shell runtime path compatibility
value: Windows Node receives native path syntax while POSIX Node retains POSIX paths
why_now: Native review found a distinct upstream mixed-runtime compatibility concern while validating CodSpeed bundle admission
parent: pm-qwoy
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: "Renew every pnpm pin to11.28.5, derive complete host-specific audited launchers from the actual installation, and exercise native external-dependency and argument controls."
expected_result: "Windows Git Bash/Cygwin native Node and CMD/PowerShell launchers resolve dependencies and preserve supported arguments/percent paths without changing source-integrity, cooldown or quality budgets."
actual_result: "All three linked checks pass at existing deadlines. CI39096420681 passes native Git Bash/Cygwin/CMD/PowerShell regressions, all installed platform consumers and100/100/100/100 coverage. Archived setup2.937 is byte-identical by independently verified SHA512; workflow contract and documented renewal preserve signatures. Serialized local SDK import, CLI transport, graph/history and mutation gates pass. CodSpeed neutral report retains its changed-runtime warning and unchanged-code pagination measurement; no acknowledgement or threshold relaxation."
component: toolchain/generated-command-shims
