comments[11]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-03T03:44:58.496Z","harness:codex","Duplicate check: complete all-status keyword NODE_PATH returns exactly four records (current CodSpeed owner, completed snapshot owner, completed MCP Apps refresh, and completed plugin-runtime owner); exact 11.28.1 returns zero without omissions. Full current pnpm bootstrap and terminal foundation metadata were read, and bootstrap history verifies. These historical completed fixes remain completed. Existing open/in-progress lists and canonical orientation were refreshed before creation. This queued intake records an upstream installer boundary rather than treating comparison templates as executable repository launchers."
  "2026-10-18T02:53:16.568Z","harness:codex","Start combined dependency-tooling renewal with pm-38w3ii. Strict all-status intake read 2991/2991 items with zero omissions, unreadable rows or active claims; canonical full metadata/history for both deferred owners was verified. Public registry selects supported pnpm 11.28.5 (2026-10-06T05:23:58.800Z), older than seven days; inspect real published generator and installed launchers before renewing comparison templates. Retain all audited CodSpeed bundle bytes, source maps, native payload, security gates and supported runtimes."
  "2026-10-18T02:57:50.433Z","harness:codex","Published pnpm 11.28.5 requires Node >=22.13, compatible with the documented >=22.18.0 floor. Its package changelog confirms Windows NODE_PATH, Cygwin target routing and CMD percent escaping repairs. Actual bundled generator source now emits distinct POSIX and Windows-installed shell programs; renew complete comparison data from that source and require only the host-appropriate program. A normal frozen install retained old launchers, so clean relinking is required to qualify the new generator; no old-launcher fallback will be accepted."
  "2026-10-18T03:06:08.060Z","harness:codex","First updated focused cohort passes 33 tests across real installed-bundle admission, isolated launcher dependency lookup, recovery grammar and workflow policy. Native actionlint 1.7.12 was downloaded from its official immutable release and admitted by the repository-pinned SHA256 before execution; all workflows pass. Clean frozen relink leaves the lockfile unchanged before the separate Sentry patch. An isolated pre-renewal complete comparator refuses the actual new launchers as expected; renewed complete comparison passes with all existing bundle hashes and inventory intact. Native Git Bash/Cygwin/CMD/PowerShell acceptance remains mandatory in the exact-head Windows job."
  "2026-10-18T03:39:18.190Z","harness:codex","Native first-head acceptance passes complete installed-bundle admission and the Git Bash/Cygwin/PowerShell external-dependency controls. CMD alone refuses the harness command because Node automatically escapes its already-authored cmd.exe command line. Use the Windows verbatim-argument transport for that explicit CMD invocation, preserving positive dependency/percent-path assertions and the old-expansion negative control. CodeRabbit completed full review of02d187e with zero actionable comments; Sourcery quota, Greptile expired trial and Cubic monthly limit are recorded as unavailable reviews, not approvals."
  "2026-10-18T03:40:07.449Z","harness:codex","CodSpeed first-head report is preserved: decodeQueryCursor measured242.1us on main versus339.9us on02d187e with a reported28.76percent regression. Chrome inspection of the actual comparison shows CPU changed fromAMD EPYC7763 toEPYC9V74 and the native-core path changed with the pnpm peer-context key while its build identity stayed574e1ea5495a22829428f4c8cc4bd474ffc7c710; the provider explicitly flags different runtime environments. Pagination source and benchmark blobs are identical between reviewed base and candidate. No performance threshold is changed and no regression is acknowledged away. A fresh revised-head benchmark and matched-context investigation remain part of review; this heterogeneous comparison alone is not proof of a code regression or of acceptable performance."
  "2026-10-18T03:41:11.025Z","harness:codex","Local static chain passes dependencies, complete bundle inventory, lint/duplication, workflow permissions/cooldown, generated contracts/skills, SDK contracts, grammar, token/recovery/PM and surface gates, then refuses the aggregate SDK import median567ms against the unchanged500ms ceiling. Its controls are45/38ms, so this is a preserved qualified product-budget failure and not a passing static verdict. The first-head hosted static failure was separately missing PM metadata; revised-head hosted static and a fresh full local run remain required after source fixes."
  "2026-10-18T04:12:42.076Z","harness:codex","Revised-head CI39095400572 correctly caught an unquoted CMD caller expression: the launcher resolved its external sentinel, but the harness split the expanded three-word value into three arguments. Quote the expression while retaining the expected single argument and the deliberate broken-launcher refusal. Git Bash/Cygwin/PowerShell and the complete bundle audit passed; do not weaken these controls. Local static validation also caught two newly prose-named item pairs; both are now truthful typed related edges through PM. The unchanged graph ceiling passes again, and the SDK import-cost gate now passes under the unchanged budget."
  "2026-10-18T04:14:40.349Z","harness:codex","Exact source CI39095400572 passed all four coverage shards and the unchanged aggregate gate: 100/100/100/100, zero uncovered counts. Corrected local launcher file passes 6 Linux controls; final artifact gate passes with 19,153,083 first-party bytes and 23,402,553 runtime bytes/4,755 runtime files. A local transport-floor run overlapped artifact rebuilding and failed qualified product budgets (get399>362ms, context459>433ms, create411>398ms; control50ms within106ms). This failed verdict is retained; a fresh serialized measurement will decide admission without changing thresholds. Chrome confirms CodSpeed revised head9575d9c still reports decodeQueryCursor242.1→339.8us with different-runtime warning (native build identical, peer-context path changed); source/benchmark blobs unchanged, no regression acknowledgement or threshold change."
  "2026-10-18T04:33:06.906Z","harness:codex","Accepted CodeRabbit inline4305703988: pin the archived Cygwin setup2.937 URL. Official archive lists2026-02-28T20:22 and its sha512.sum matches the exact existing6acea47c…c5aafcc digest; independently downloaded archived bytes match too. Therefore native cohort39096420681 uses the same verified executable bytes. Add the versioned URL to the existing workflow contract and document controlled renewal without weakening default package signatures. That source head passed all hosted CI jobs, including Git Bash/Cygwin/CMD/PowerShell and100/100/100/100 coverage; only required external codecov/patch was absent in the settled receipt."
  "2026-10-18T04:38:50.013Z","harness:codex",Final package-owned generation and --check pass with the latest registry pm-changelog2026.10.16 and four new changelog entries. Deep package doctor returns ok with zero activation failures and all4 active project extensions loaded; it retains an explicit partial-update-health warning because the npm changelog source has no recorded update check. Independently verified npm latest and installed extension are both2026.10.16; do not describe that warning as a clean doctor result. Full live history validation checks2993 items with zero drift; the same170 historical resolution-field warnings remain.
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-10-03T03:46:55.503Z","harness:codex","Boundary: these .txt files are validation references, while the installed pnpm/@zkochan generator writes the executable launchers. Preserve complete program admission and unchanged cooldown; do not edit reference bytes to invent new generated output. The official pnpm release documents related CMD percent-path and Cygwin target fixes, but resolution of the specific POSIX NODE_PATH plus Windows node.exe combination must be demonstrated with actual installed runtime controls before adopting a candidate."
